.TH GETPROTOBYNAME_R 3
.SH NAME
getprotobyname_r, getprotobynumber_r, getprotoent_r \- reentrant network protocol database lookups
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netdb.h>
.PP
.BI "int getprotobyname_r(const char *" name ", struct protoent *" ret ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct protoent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getprotobynumber_r(int " proto ", struct protoent *" ret ,
.BI "char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct protoent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getprotoent_r(struct protoent *" ret ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ,
.BI "struct protoent **" result ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the reentrant equivalents of
.BR getprotobyname (3),
.BR getprotobynumber (3)
and
.BR getprotoent (3).
The matching
.I /etc/protocols
entry is copied into the caller-supplied
.I ret
structure and scratch buffer
.IR buf
(length
.IR buflen );
.I *result
points at
.I ret
on success or is NULL when no entry matches.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success, or ERANGE if
.I buf
is too small.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I buf
was too small to hold the result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getprotoent (3),
.BR getservbyname_r (3),
.BR getnetbyname_r (3)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
